@startuml
title POST /api/ai-agents-teams/{address}/{id}/publish-to-firesky/prepare + /send — give a deployed team a social account
skinparam backgroundColor #F8FBFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam ArrowColor #294C60
skinparam sequence {
  ParticipantBackgroundColor #EAF5FF
  ParticipantBorderColor #38789E
  LifeLineBorderColor #6A92AA
  GroupBackgroundColor #FFF3E8
  GroupBorderColor #D97638
}

actor "Team owner" as Owner #FFD8C2
participant "AgentsTeamsApiSdk\n.publishToFiresky(id, req)" as SDK #D5EAF7
participant "EmbersEvents\n(WebSocket)" as Events #E3D8F5
participant "Embers API" as API #FFC9A8
participant "AgentsTeamsService" as Domain #CDEACC
participant "F1r3sky\n(PDS)" as Firesky #FFDFC4
participant "F1r3node\nchain + observer" as Chain #FFE4A6

Owner -> SDK : publishToFiresky(id, { pds_url, email,\n  handle, password, invite_code? })

group Phase 1 — prepare (account work happens here)
SDK -> API : POST .../{address}/{id}/publish-to-firesky/prepare
API -> Domain : prepare publication
Domain -> Firesky : create or log into the account\n(handle, email, password, invite code)
Domain -> Firesky : mint a per-publication app password\n(numbered from the names present:\n"Embers", "Embers 2", ...)
Domain -> Firesky : write the com.f1r3sky.agentsteam.config\nrecord naming the CURRENT deployment URI
Firesky --> Domain : account ready (did, handle)
Domain -> Domain : render the contract pushing the\nENCRYPTED credential onto the\nteam's on-chain credential stack
Domain --> API : PublishToFireskyResp { contract }
API --> SDK : PrepareResponse { response, token }
end

group Sign, subscribe, send
SDK -> SDK : signed = signContract(contract, privateKey)
SDK -> Events : subscribeForDeploy(\n  hex(signed.sig).toLowerCase(), maxWait)
SDK -> API : POST .../publish-to-firesky/send\n{ prepare_request, prepare_response,\n  request: signed, token }
API -> API : verify the echo hash binding
API -> Domain : deploy signed contract
Domain -> Chain : deploy (credential push)
Chain --> Domain : accepted
API <-- Domain : deploy id
SDK <-- API : 200 SendResp { deploy_id }
SDK --> Owner : { prepareResponse, sendResponse,\n  waitForFinalization }
end

group Finalization — observed on the WebSocket
Chain --> Events : Finalized { deploy_id, ...,\n  node_type: Observer }
Events --> Owner : waitForFinalization resolves
end

note over API #FAD8D8
The prepare request carries PDS credentials
(email, password, optional invite code) to the
service. What reaches the chain is an encrypted
per-publication app password, never the account
password; still, treat this endpoint as a
credential boundary and only ever call it over
HTTPS against a service you trust.
end note

note over Domain #FFF0C7
Publication is keyed by DEPLOYMENT URI, not team
id: the config record names whichever deployment
was current at publish time. Re-deploying mints
a new URI, which is what published-state's
is_latest_deployment reports on.
end note
@enduml
